    "body": "### What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nWhen using verl, we needed to customize the exported safetensor shard size (e.g., saving in 5GB shards), but verl provided no configuration seam for HF transformers `save_pretrained` in the checkpoint manager. Rather than add a one-off shard-size field, this PR exposes the kwargs mapping so users can compose any HF transformers `save_pretrained` customization supported by their installed Transformers version.\r\n\r\nExpose an optional `hf_save_pretrained_kwargs` mapping for Hugging Face model exports written by `FSDPCheckpointManager`. The mapping is forwarded directly to Transformers [`PreTrainedModel.save_pretrained`](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/main/src/transformers/modeling_utils.py#L3235-L3248). When it is `null`, verl forwards no extra keyword arguments and preserves the installed Transformers defaults; `max_shard_size` is the motivating example rather than a special verl field.\r\n\r\nThis applies only to in-training `hf_model` exports through `FSDPCheckpointManager` (FSDP and VeOmni). Standalone `verl.model_merger` is out of scope because it has its own CLI and `ModelMergerConfig`; Megatron merger exports use a separate sharding path and are unchanged.\r\n\r\nRelated issues #298 and #533 document demand for deployable Hugging Face checkpoints. This does not duplicate #1288, which added direct FSDP Hugging Face export but did not expose `save_pretrained` kwargs. The open-PR searches found no other PR adding this general configuration seam.\r\n\r\nFixes one part of https://github.com/verl-project/verl/issues/8027\r\n\r\n### Checklist Before Starting\r\n\r\n- [x] Search for similar PRs: https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=is%3Apr+is%3Aopen+max_shard_size\r\n- [x] Format the PR title as `[{modules}] {type}: {description}`.\r\n\r\n### API and Usage Example\r\n\r\n`hf_save_pretrained_kwargs` is consumed only when the checkpoint includes an `hf_model` export. For example:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# PPO actor, with either the FSDP or VeOmni engine\r\nactor_rollout_ref.actor.checkpoint.hf_save_pretrained_kwargs='{max_shard_size:5GB}'\r\n\r\n# SFT, with engine=fsdp or engine=veomni\r\ncheckpoint.hf_save_pretrained_kwargs='{max_shard_size:5GB}'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe critic YAML intentionally omits this field because standalone HF critic exports are uncommon; opt in with `+critic.checkpoint.hf_save_pretrained_kwargs='{max_shard_size:5GB}'`.\r\n\r\nWhen `hf_save_pretrained_kwargs` is `null`, verl passes no extra arguments to `save_pretrained`; otherwise it forwards the configured mapping unchanged.\r\n\r\n### Test\r\n\r\nSix 8-GPU training runs with `Qwen/Qwen3-8B` verified `hf_save_pretrained_kwargs=null` and the `max_shard_size:5GB` override across FSDP actor, SFT, and VeOmni actor. Each export contains FP32 tensors (the current default), has the expected `8,190,735,360` parameters, and reloads through Transformers:\r\n\r\n| Path | Export dtype | Default | `5GB` | HF reload |\r\n|---|---|---:|---:|---|\r\n| FSDP actor | FP32 (default) | 1 file | 7 shards | Passed |\r\n| SFT | FP32 (default) | 1 file | 7 shards | Passed |\r\n| VeOmni actor | FP32 (default) | 1 file | 7 shards | Passed |\r\n\r\n### Checklist Before Submitting\r\n\r\n- [x] Read the Contribute Guide.\r\n- [x] Apply relevant pre-commit checks.\r\n- [x] Add / update documentation.\r\n- [x] Test coverage considered: no permanent test was added because this is a thin pass-through. The multi-GPU runs above verified default and configured sharding behavior end to end.\r\n- [x] Send a message in the `ci-request` channel once human review is complete.\r\n- [x] This PR does not touch the `recipe` submodule.\r\n\r\nAI assistance from OpenAI Codex was used for code-path analysis, implementation, validation, experiment orchestration, and PR drafting. I can confirm I have reviewed every changed line.\r\n",
